---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import VersionHeader from "../../components/VersionHeader.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../site-config";

// The site's final content page. Ungraded, and deliberately not shaped like
// an assessment: no rubric, no weight, no due date. Framing, then the
// prompt, then the four artefacts the student already has.

const artefacts = [
  {
    href: "/assessments/duplicate-audit/",
    title: "The Duplicate Audit",
    produced: "A genealogy of one family of your own files, and the relationships you could not establish.",
  },
  {
    href: "/assessments/which-one-is-real/",
    title: "Which One Is Real?",
    produced: "A reconstructed timeline, and a verdict with a ground stated for it.",
  },
  {
    href: "/assessments/merge-conflict-in-writing/",
    title: "Merge Conflict, In Writing",
    produced: "A merged document, and a rationale recording what was cut and why.",
  },
  {
    href: "/assessments/format-autopsy/",
    title: "Format Autopsy",
    produced: "A chain of converted artefacts, and a verdict on where the file stopped being itself.",
  },
];
---

<ContentLayout
  title="The Version History"
  description="The last entry in the file. Ungraded, and not a fifth assessment: a reading of your own semester's evidence against the claim the course opened with."
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <VersionHeader
    version="1.1"
    status="CURRENT"
    history={[{ version: "1.0", note: "Copyedited for house style." }]}
  />

  <p>
    The course opened by claiming there is no such thing as &ldquo;the
    file.&rdquo; Over twelve weeks you produced four pieces of evidence
    against that claim, or for it. This page is where you read them back.
  </p>

  <p>Nothing is submitted here and nothing is marked.</p>

  <blockquote class="closing-prompt">
    <p>
      Across your own semester&rsquo;s evidence, what actually decided which
      version counted, and was it ever really the file itself?
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>What you have</h2>

  <ul class="closing-artefacts">
    {
      artefacts.map((artefact) => (
        <li>
          <a href={withBase(artefact.href)}>{artefact.title}</a>
          <span>{artefact.produced}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <p>
    Read the four together rather than in turn. In each one you reached a
    point where the files stopped answering and you decided anyway. Find
    those four moments and put them side by side. They are the only places
    in the semester where the question was actually settled, and none of
    them was settled by the bytes.
  </p>

  <p>
    Note what you were relying on at each of them. The four grounds from
    week 8 are one vocabulary for it, and they are not the only one. What
    matters is whether you can now say which ground you used, rather than
    reporting that one version was newer and treating that as an answer.
  </p>

  <h2>Case closed</h2>

  <p>
    Every system in this course reported something true and insufficient. A
    filename asserted finality it could not enforce. A hash proved identity
    and settled nothing. A diff reported the differences and declined the
    judgement. A sync service picked the later timestamp because it had
    nothing else. A conversion succeeded and dropped the comments without
    saying so.
  </p>

  <p>
    None of them was broken. They answered the questions they could answer.
    The remaining question (which of these is the one that counts) was
    never a question about files, which is why twelve weeks of looking at
    files could only ever bring you to the edge of it.
  </p>

  <p class="closing-signoff">
    Write it down somewhere you will find it again. Unlike most of what this
    course examined, that part is under your control.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .closing-prompt {
    margin-block: 1.5rem;
    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
    border-inline-start: 4px solid var(--at-primary);
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-h4, 1.15rem);
  }

  .closing-prompt p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .closing-artefacts {
    margin-block: 0 1.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .closing-artefacts li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding-block: 0.6rem;
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--at-divider);
  }

  .closing-artefacts li:last-child {
    border-block-end: 0;
  }

  .closing-artefacts span {
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
  }

  .closing-signoff {
    margin-block-start: 2rem;
    padding-block-start: 1rem;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--at-divider);
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }
</style>
